---
import SiteFooter from '@/components/SiteFooter.astro'
import SiteHeader from '@/components/SiteHeader.astro'
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro'
import { CHECKOUT, PRICE, SITE } from '@/lib/site'

/// Nothing is for sale until there is a build to install, and the page says which
/// state it is in rather than showing a button that goes nowhere.
const onSale = CHECKOUT.url !== null

const updateWindow = [
  {
    claim: 'Every build released in your year activates, and stays activated.',
    detail:
      'Whatever its version number. A major release inside your window is yours the same way a patch is, and it keeps working for good.',
  },
  {
    claim: 'When the year is up, nothing stops working.',
    detail:
      'Your last covered version stays fully licensed, with no limit and no nagging. There is no subscription to cancel because there was never one to start.',
  },
  {
    claim: 'Only a newer build asks for a renewal.',
    detail:
      'Install something released after your window and the app says so and runs on the free tier. Go back to a covered build and it is licensed again. The check happens on your machine, with no network.',
  },
]
---

<Base
  title={`Pricing: ${SITE.name}`}
  description="One licence, bought once, with twelve months of updates. What the free tier does, what a licence lifts, and exactly what a year of updates means."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
    <SiteHeader />

    <!-- Direct children only: as a descendant selector this prose spacing reaches
         into the price card and the grid below, and it outweighs their own margins. -->
    <main class="py-14 [&>h2]:mt-12 [&>h2]:font-mono [&>h2]:text-lg [&>h2]:font-medium [&>h2]:tracking-tight [&>p]:mt-4 [&>p]:leading-relaxed">
      <p class="label">Pricing</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 font-mono text-2xl leading-snug font-semibold tracking-tight">
        Bought once. Yours for good.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-mute">
        One edition, no tiers to compare, and no subscription. You pay once, you get twelve months
        of updates, and the version you end on keeps working forever. Building it yourself from
        source stays free, so what a licence buys is the signed builds and the work behind them.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 rounded-card border border-rule bg-wash px-6 py-6">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="font-mono text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
              {PRICE.licence}
              <span class="text-base font-medium text-mute">{PRICE.currency}</span>
            </p>
            <p class="mt-1 font-mono text-xs text-mute">
              once, then {PRICE.renewal} a year if you want newer builds
            </p>
          </div>
          {
            onSale
              ? (
                  <a
                    href={CHECKOUT.url}
                    data-umami-event={CHECKOUT.event}
                    class="rounded-card bg-ink px-5 py-2.5 font-mono text-sm font-medium text-paper underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
                  >Buy a licence</a
                  >
                )
              : (
                  <p class="font-mono text-xs text-mute">
                    Not on sale yet. There is no build to install first.
                  </p>
                )
          }
        </div>

        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3 border-t border-rule pt-6">
          <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-px w-4 shrink-0 bg-rule" />
            <span>Every feature, every engine, agent access included.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-px w-4 shrink-0 bg-rule" />
            <span>{PRICE.months} months of updates, and the version you end on is yours to keep.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-px w-4 shrink-0 bg-rule" />
            <span>One person, every machine you work on. Not a seat per laptop.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2.5 h-px w-4 shrink-0 bg-rule" />
            <span>macOS, Windows and Linux, signed and updating themselves.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Free, with one limit</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        The app runs without a licence, for as long as you like, and the only thing it holds back is
        how many workspace tabs you can open: {PRICE.freeTabs} per connection. Nothing else is
        withheld. Every engine, the SQL editor, tunnels, export, and the MCP server that lends
        databases to coding agents all work on the free tier, because a differentiator you cannot
        try is not one.
      </p>
      <p class="text-mute">
        That limit is deliberately the one you meet while working rather than while judging. Adding
        connections costs nothing and opening one is enough to explore; it is comparing two tables
        with a query open beside them that runs out of room.
      </p>

      <h2>What a year of updates means</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        This is the part people get burned by elsewhere, so here it is exactly:
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-px">
        {
          updateWindow.map(item => (
            <div class="border-t border-rule py-6 sm:grid sm:grid-cols-[18rem_1fr] sm:gap-8">
              <h3 class="font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed font-medium">{item.claim}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mute sm:mt-0">{item.detail}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="text-mute">
        A renewal at {PRICE.renewal} moves the window forward another {PRICE.months} months. You are
        never charged automatically, and letting it lapse costs you nothing you already had.
      </p>

      <h2>Your licence, and your machines</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        After buying you get a licence key. Paste it into the app once and it fetches a signed
        licence file, which is what the app actually checks, offline, from then on. No account, no
        sign-in, and no call home to keep working.
      </p>
      <p class="text-mute">
        The licence is per person rather than per machine: activating your key issues that file, up
        to {PRICE.activations} times, and the file works wherever you put it. Copying the one you
        already have to another machine of yours costs nothing, and you can release an activation
        from your account if you run out.
      </p>

      <h2>Before you buy</h2>
      <p class="text-mute">
        The
        <a
          href="/terms"
          data-umami-event="terms-pricing"
          class="text-ink underline underline-offset-4"
        >terms of sale</a
        > cover the licence, the update window and refunds. Anything unclear, ask first:
        <a
          href="mailto:hi@soquel.dev"
          data-umami-event="contact-pricing"
          class="text-ink underline underline-offset-4"
        >hi@soquel.dev</a
        >.
      </p>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Base>
